1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
(EP08 Behind-the-Scenes)

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:10,980
(Heart-Thumping Couple Ranking:
Special Surprise)

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:16,430
There are blue flowers here.

5
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:18,130
So many colors.

6
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:20,280
Do you remember this place?

7
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,480
Of course.

8
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:24,150
We had our first date here.

9
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:24,730
Yes.

10
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:27,190
We'll make these

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:27,910
(Materials for kites)
little kites

12
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,900
and plant dyes.

13
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:29,460
(Botanical dyeing)

14
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:31,210
We'll unlock them through some games.

15
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:31,940
(SiYi couple Pictionary)

16
00:00:31,960 --> 00:00:32,760
(Draw a question for each round.)

17
00:00:32,770 --> 00:00:33,590
(Draw your answer at the same time.)

18
00:00:33,590 --> 00:00:34,400
(If you fail
to guess your partner's answer,)

19
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:35,180
(you'll be punished.)

20
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:35,980
(Complete the game
to unlock two pairs of kites.)

21
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,350
Where's the question card?

22
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,110
Right here.

23
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:40,780
(Flips to look)

24
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:42,210
Why are you peeking?

25
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:45,110
You do it.

26
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:46,030
You go first.

27
00:00:48,760 --> 00:00:51,350
(Question)
The best food you've eaten recently.

28
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,620
(Glances)

29
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:53,710
I have one in mind.

30
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,200
I had it yesterday.

31
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,190
And the day before.

32
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:57,670
Really?

33
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:58,590
Three days ago too.

34
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:01,540
(Giving the answer through eye contact)

35
00:01:02,580 --> 00:01:03,980
(Got it)

36
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,560
Sure. Let's start.

37
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:10,180
(Glances)

38
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:12,180
Why did you pick this color too?

39
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:13,620
(Both pick pink)
Could we be drawing

40
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:13,900
Could we...

41
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:14,670
the same thing?

42
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:16,320
Woah.

43
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:28,140
(Glances)

44
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:29,230
It makes my hand look so dark.

45
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:32,340
(Can't hold it in)

46
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:34,260
(Demonstrating)

47
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:36,840
Really. I've been staring at my hand.

48
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:37,870
I can't take it anymore.

49
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,790
It's the same tone as my jacket.

50
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:41,460
(Makes skin look dark)

51
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,460
(Can't stop laughing)

52
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,670
The kite is white.
Makes the tan stand out.

53
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,310
You're not tan.

54
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:50,740
(Stares)

55
00:01:54,870 --> 00:01:55,300
I'm done.

56
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:56,190
Me too.

57
00:01:56,410 --> 00:01:56,780
Alright.

58
00:01:58,720 --> 00:01:59,550
Can you guess

59
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:00,820
what I drew?

60
00:02:00,840 --> 00:02:02,100
That's a bubble tea.

61
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:03,370
(Bubble tea)
This is mutton.

62
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:04,100
(Mutton)
Yes.

63
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,530
(Milk skin)
This is milk skin.

64
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,100
(Got all correct)
Yes.

65
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,220
(Bubble tea, milk skin, mutton)

66
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:10,380
So smart.

67
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:10,820
(Praises)

68
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:14,650
What you drew

69
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:16,180
is also the milk skin.

70
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,070
(Milk skin)

71
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:17,910
Biscuit.

72
00:02:18,260 --> 00:02:18,980
(Biscuit)

73
00:02:18,980 --> 00:02:21,180
And this is the milk cube.

74
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:21,810
(Milk cube)

75
00:02:21,810 --> 00:02:22,620
This is a yogurt cube.

76
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:23,260
(Yogurt cube)

77
00:02:23,260 --> 00:02:23,890
This is bubble tea.

78
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:24,460
(Bubble tea)

79
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:25,940
And this is a cheese stick.

80
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:26,620
(Cheese stick)

81
00:02:27,010 --> 00:02:27,600
You got it right.

82
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:28,620
(Got it all right. Milk skin, biscuit,
cheese, milk cube, milk tea, yogurt cube)

83
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:30,300
(Challenge successful)

84
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,630
Telepathy.

85
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:37,680
Let's see who gets

86
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:39,650
to draw this perfect kite.

87
00:02:39,650 --> 00:02:41,070
A masterpiece by Baoding Van Gogh.

88
00:02:42,320 --> 00:02:43,140
I'm not.

89
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,290
Next one then.

90
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:46,160
Next one.

91
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,540
Draw a card.

92
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:52,560
(Question)
Your favorite thing to do in the house.

93
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:54,050
Let's start.

94
00:02:54,050 --> 00:02:55,230
(Blocks view)
You can't look at mine.

95
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:55,870
I won't.

96
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:57,340
(Defending)

97
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:04,220
(Sneaks a peek)

98
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:06,620
(Catches him)

99
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:11,670
(Covers)
Don't peek at mine.

100
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:14,660
(Defending)

101
00:03:14,660 --> 00:03:15,950
How am I supposed to block you?

102
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:19,740
(Trying not to laugh)

103
00:03:22,180 --> 00:03:23,000
I'm done.

104
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:23,920
Me too.

105
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,430
Let me guess.

106
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,830
Playing badminton?

107
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:27,990
No.

108
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,030
Cooking?

109
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:30,270
No.

110
00:03:31,030 --> 00:03:31,460
What is it?

111
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:34,460
(Trying again)
Go for a drive?

112
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:35,030
No.

113
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:36,990
Chatting?

114
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,030
No.

115
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,110
Dreaming?

116
00:03:40,270 --> 00:03:40,890
Dreaming.

117
00:03:42,430 --> 00:03:43,560
Did you have too much to drink?

118
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:44,320
No.

119
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,540
(Joking around)

120
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:51,100
(Sneaks a peek)

121
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:57,540
(Laughs)

122
00:03:57,540 --> 00:03:58,630
Eating breakfast.

123
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:03,370
You saw something, didn't you?

124
00:04:03,620 --> 00:04:04,620
(Denying)
I didn't.

125
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,070
Yours is about breakfast.

126
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:06,620
No.

127
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:07,880
Just eating then.

128
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:08,950
Yes.

129
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,260
(Wu Siying's answer: Eating)

130
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:10,970
I said it earlier.

131
00:04:10,970 --> 00:04:11,510
You said no.

132
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,390
You guessed cooking.

133
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,070
I did.

134
00:04:13,070 --> 00:04:14,110
But not eating.

135
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,040
Cooking.

136
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,320
Fine. You won't get this right.

137
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:21,730
Give it a go.

138
00:04:22,490 --> 00:04:23,270
Stargazing room.

139
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:23,960
Go on a date.

140
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:25,020
Go for a walk.

141
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,350
Did I get any of it right?

142
00:04:26,820 --> 00:04:27,660
(Anticipates)

143
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:29,230
No.

144
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:31,870
I...

145
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:33,580
(Yihang's answer: Making eye contact)
Because I drew us having eye contact.

146
00:04:33,680 --> 00:04:34,320
You got it all wrong.

147
00:04:34,790 --> 00:04:35,310
What do we do?

148
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:36,350
Accept the punishment together.

149
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:38,310
For the punishment,

150
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:40,490
(Punishment)
name one of your partner's flaws or quirks.

151
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:42,100
Once I say it,
you have to admit it's true.

152
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:43,380
You go first.

153
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:45,560
I think

154
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:47,990
you're a little too blunt sometimes.

155
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,510
A little too blunt?

156
00:04:49,520 --> 00:04:50,430
Do you agree?

157
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,100
Yes. I admit it.

158
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:51,580
(Instantly agrees)

159
00:04:51,850 --> 00:04:52,580
Yes. I admit it.

160
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:54,020
It's my turn now.

161
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,310
You take forever in the bathroom.

162
00:04:57,820 --> 00:04:59,500
(Warning look)

163
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:00,660
(Pinches)

164
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,340
I didn't say anything.

165
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,020
(Backs down)

166
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:09,980
(Starting over)
But you guessed it wrong too.

167
00:05:09,980 --> 00:05:11,730
You have to name a flaw or little quirk.

168
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:17,940
(Restarts)

169
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,460
Your flaw is that you're too skinny.

170
00:05:21,900 --> 00:05:22,460
(Oh)

171
00:05:22,930 --> 00:05:23,560
I don't agree.

172
00:05:25,680 --> 00:05:26,990
(Third attempt)
Didn't you guess it wrong?

173
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:27,590
No. I'm thinking.

174
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,030
You have to name a flaw or little quirk.

175
00:05:30,220 --> 00:05:31,660
(Restarts)

176
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:32,700
(Glances)

177
00:05:33,620 --> 00:05:34,870
(Finally gets it)
A little quirk.

178
00:05:36,090 --> 00:05:36,860
A little quirk.

179
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:38,300
You like to pretend to be a zombie.

180
00:05:38,740 --> 00:05:39,450
Pretend to be a zombie.

181
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:40,540
(Subtitles have left the chat)

182
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:43,180
(Agrees)
Sure.

183
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:44,900
Alright. We're done with this.

184
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,470
Let's do the botanical dye.

185
00:05:48,640 --> 00:05:49,630
Let's make up a new rule.

186
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:52,220
(Winner gets to choose a plant dye first)
Rock goes like this.

187
00:05:53,860 --> 00:05:54,780
(Shy)

188
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:55,790
What's rock?

189
00:05:56,140 --> 00:05:56,620
(Asking on purpose)

190
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:57,940
Rock.

191
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:58,830
This is rock.

192
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:00,360
This is scissors.

193
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:01,820
This is paper.

194
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,840
(Does it again)
This is paper.

195
00:06:04,300 --> 00:06:05,460
(Amused)

196
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:08,270
Did you get it?

197
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,410
No.

198
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:10,140
(Teasing)

199
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,180
This is rock.

200
00:06:11,940 --> 00:06:12,880
This is scissors.

201
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:14,930
This is paper.

202
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,710
Teach me again.

203
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:21,820
Rock.

204
00:06:21,820 --> 00:06:22,940
(Copies him)
Rock.

205
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:24,250
Scissors.

206
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:25,620
Paper.

207
00:06:25,740 --> 00:06:26,310
Okay.

208
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:27,140
Alright.

209
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:30,960
Let's start.

210
00:06:32,060 --> 00:06:32,700
(Starting)

211
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:33,050
Rock.

212
00:06:33,050 --> 00:06:34,390
Rock, paper, scissors.

213
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,500
(Scissors, rock)

214
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:36,480
I won.

215
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:38,150
I want green.

216
00:06:38,230 --> 00:06:38,670
Okay.

217
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Rock, paper, scissors.

218
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:42,060
(Scissors)

219
00:06:42,060 --> 00:06:44,020
Rock, paper, scissors.

220
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,230
(Rock, scissors)
I won.

221
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:46,400
You get to pick now.

222
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,950
I want the blue one.

223
00:06:47,960 --> 00:06:49,470
The blue? Sure.

224
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,730
One last round.

225
00:06:51,360 --> 00:06:53,150
Rock, paper, scissors.

226
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:54,380
(Scissors, paper)

227
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:55,310
- I lost.
- I won.

228
00:06:55,960 --> 00:06:57,310
I want this one.

229
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:58,170
Sure.

230
00:06:58,880 --> 00:06:59,630
What do you want to make?

231
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:02,170
Something beautiful.

232
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,110
Beautiful.

233
00:07:03,660 --> 00:07:04,940
Everyone will like it.

234
00:07:05,710 --> 00:07:06,700
I'm sure they will.

235
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:12,940
(Leans in for a closer look)

236
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:14,230
Do you know what this is?

237
00:07:14,230 --> 00:07:14,730
What's this?

238
00:07:15,620 --> 00:07:16,730
These are fallen leaves.

239
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:18,990
I thought it was
crispy sweet-and-sour pork.

240
00:07:19,160 --> 00:07:20,350
They're fallen leaves.

241
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,830
Fall's almost here.

242
00:07:24,810 --> 00:07:25,730
Mine is really cool.

243
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:27,800
Super cool.

244
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:35,520
Look at what I made.

245
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,030
Guess what it is.

246
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:38,700
(Cui Yihang's work)
Can you guess it?

247
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:40,870
This is the roasted mutton leg
you had yesterday.

248
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:41,870
What mutton leg?

249
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:42,910
What is it then?

250
00:07:42,990 --> 00:07:43,700
A swing.

251
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:44,650
Swing?

252
00:07:44,730 --> 00:07:46,560
(Leaves and swing)
These are leaves and a swing.

253
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:48,030
You should stamp two little figures

254
00:07:48,030 --> 00:07:49,200
on it.

255
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:49,950
Two figures?

256
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:51,630
Great idea.

257
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,910
I'll redo this one.

258
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:56,700
(Continues to work on it)

259
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:02,850
Here.

260
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:06,710
Careful with your hand.

261
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:10,960
These two figures.

262
00:08:12,140 --> 00:08:14,060
(Swing)

263
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:15,700
Alright. Let's make one together.

264
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,090
I'm hitting you.

265
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,000
You are?

266
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,760
I'll hit you then.

267
00:08:39,150 --> 00:08:40,670
I need to hit it harder.

268
00:08:48,490 --> 00:08:49,200
Done.

269
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:51,110
(Rowing)

270
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,410
I have a game suggestion.

271
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:54,030
What game?

272
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,390
A few days ago, didn't we play

273
00:08:56,390 --> 00:08:57,840
(Suggests playing Tour the Three Gardens)
Tour the Three Gardens?

274
00:08:58,180 --> 00:09:00,310
The loser draws one of these.

275
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:01,060
(Loser draws a punishment slip)

276
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:02,590
There's a punishment inside.

277
00:09:02,590 --> 00:09:03,020
Sure.

278
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:03,960
(SiYi couple Tour the Three Gardens)

279
00:09:03,960 --> 00:09:04,470
(Pick a garden.)

280
00:09:04,470 --> 00:09:05,200
(Take turns naming things
in the garden.)

281
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,070
(No repeats or hesitations.)

282
00:09:06,070 --> 00:09:06,820
(The loser has to draw
a dialect challenge.)

283
00:09:06,840 --> 00:09:07,540
(Complete the challenge
to unlock 13 pairs of botanical dyes.)

284
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:08,470
There are so many flowers.

285
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,390
Let's tour the garden.

286
00:09:09,880 --> 00:09:10,550
The garden?

287
00:09:11,680 --> 00:09:12,230
Sure.

288
00:09:12,740 --> 00:09:13,160
Hmm.

289
00:09:23,580 --> 00:09:23,980
Alright.

290
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:25,260
(Round One officially begins)

291
00:09:26,420 --> 00:09:27,580
(Laughs along)

292
00:09:30,610 --> 00:09:31,180
For real.

293
00:09:31,180 --> 00:09:32,560
(Starting over)
Let's...

294
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,050
What?

295
00:09:34,340 --> 00:09:35,290
What were you going to say?

296
00:09:35,290 --> 00:09:36,590
How do you want to say it?

297
00:09:37,910 --> 00:09:40,060
I'll say,
"Let's tour the garden together."

298
00:09:40,650 --> 00:09:42,070
Then I'll say, "What's in the garden?"

299
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:44,960
Let's tour the garden together.

300
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,390
What's in the garden?

301
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:50,410
I'll go first.

302
00:09:50,410 --> 00:09:51,060
Yes.

303
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:53,190
There are roses in the garden.

304
00:09:53,190 --> 00:09:54,020
Chrysanthemums.

305
00:09:54,450 --> 00:09:55,320
Little chrysanthemums.

306
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,590
Begonias.

307
00:09:56,990 --> 00:09:57,640
Peonies.

308
00:09:58,550 --> 00:09:59,050
Peonies?

309
00:10:00,010 --> 00:10:01,230
Draw a punishment.

310
00:10:01,230 --> 00:10:03,020
(Cui Yihang has to take a punishment
in Round One)

311
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:06,980
(Say, "OMG, you're so freaking cute!"
in the Northeastern dialect)

312
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,340
It's a Northeastern dialect challenge.

313
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:09,510
Say it in the Northeastern accent.

314
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:10,070
I can't.

315
00:10:10,680 --> 00:10:11,470
Teach me.

316
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:12,950
Let me hear you try.

317
00:10:13,820 --> 00:10:15,370
"OMG, you're so freaking cute."

318
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:17,750
Is that right?

319
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:18,790
Who's freaking cute?

320
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,110
(Teasing)
You are.

321
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,470
Did you say so?

322
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:23,140
How about this?

323
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:25,090
"OMG,"

324
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,350
"Si is so freaking cute."

325
00:10:26,350 --> 00:10:27,550
(Si is so freaking cute)

326
00:10:27,550 --> 00:10:28,790
Si is so freaking cute.

327
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:31,470
How was that?

328
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:32,270
Pretty cute.

329
00:10:34,190 --> 00:10:35,450
Let's have another round.

330
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:36,420
Where do you want to tour?

331
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,520
The vegetable garden.

332
00:10:37,860 --> 00:10:38,640
Vegetable garden?

333
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:39,070
Yes.

334
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:39,900
Okay.

335
00:10:40,830 --> 00:10:42,340
Let's tour the vegetable garden.

336
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,680
What's in the vegetable garden?

337
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:44,710
There are eggplants.

338
00:10:44,710 --> 00:10:45,300
Rapeseed.

339
00:10:45,570 --> 00:10:46,640
Corn.

340
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,320
Potatoes.

341
00:10:47,320 --> 00:10:48,000
I said it.

342
00:10:48,040 --> 00:10:48,870
(You didn't)
You said eggplant.

343
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:49,830
I said potatoes.

344
00:10:49,830 --> 00:10:50,890
Potatoes were the first thing I said.

345
00:10:50,890 --> 00:10:51,740
(You really didn't)
You said eggplant.

346
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:52,700
I'll let you have this one.

347
00:10:52,920 --> 00:10:53,540
Fine.

348
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:54,390
You're letting me have it?

349
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:58,420
(Game continues)

350
00:10:58,420 --> 00:10:59,000
Potatoes.

351
00:10:59,000 --> 00:10:59,900
Tomatoes.

352
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:00,910
Green beans.

353
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:01,420
Cucumbers.

354
00:11:03,020 --> 00:11:03,900
(Fails again)

355
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:04,940
Here.

356
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:07,380
(Cui Yihang has to take a punishment
in Round Two)

357
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,284
(Say, "Bang bang, two punches
out of nowhere.")

358
00:11:09,284 --> 00:11:10,420
(in the Northeastern dialect)

359
00:11:10,800 --> 00:11:12,630
Bang bang, two punches out of nowhere.

360
00:11:16,780 --> 00:11:18,830
Do you know why
it doesn't sound convincing?

361
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:19,980
Say it again.

362
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,430
Bang bang...

363
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,390
You need to add some action.

364
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,340
I need to make it hurt.

365
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,350
Let's keep drawing?

366
00:11:32,350 --> 00:11:32,800
Okay.

367
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,350
Great.

368
00:11:42,340 --> 00:11:44,480
I hope they're happy
when they receive it.

369
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:47,760
They'll be happy for a whole month
when they get it.

370
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:49,190
A whole lifetime.

371
00:11:49,760 --> 00:11:50,550
That amazing?

372
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:56,470
This is everyone's love for us.

373
00:11:56,470 --> 00:11:57,420
We've received it.

374
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:58,590
Love in every color.

375
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,830
Pass it on.

376
00:12:02,800 --> 00:12:03,880
You're really earned

377
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,860
that Baoding Van Gogh title.

378
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:06,790
Pretty good, huh?

379
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,080
Yes. It's very vivid.

380
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:10,670
So impressive.

381
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,890
A four-leaf clover
is a symbol of good luck.

382
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,230
I hope everyone
can have a little more luck.

383
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:26,640
What do you think?

384
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,630
It's a great idea.

385
00:12:28,810 --> 00:12:30,790
You're such a creative girl
with so many ideas.

386
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,350
I'm done.

387
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:38,910
Where is this?

388
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:41,070
(Answers instantly)
Confession night.

389
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:42,210
Which one?

390
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,510
The mid-show confession.

391
00:12:45,210 --> 00:12:46,630
Because you were wearing black.

392
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,030
This is the flower.

393
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:49,630
What color was it?

394
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:50,360
This is the phone.

395
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:52,180
(By the sea, Si)

396
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:53,510
Write them some wishes.

397
00:12:53,510 --> 00:12:55,220
(Writing wishes for everyone)

398
00:13:08,890 --> 00:13:10,960
Let's take some polaroids to give them.

399
00:13:16,560 --> 00:13:17,400
Let's pack them up.

400
00:13:17,510 --> 00:13:17,990
Sure.

401
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,540
(Starts packing)

402
00:13:48,450 --> 00:13:49,730
We should wrap this up.

403
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:55,370
We hope those who got our presents

404
00:13:55,370 --> 00:13:56,760
can stay happy every day.

405
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:57,650
Bye bye.

406
00:13:58,160 --> 00:13:58,610
Bye bye.

407
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:00,260
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

408
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:01,940
(SVIP updates every Mon & Tue at noon)

409
00:14:01,940 --> 00:14:04,140
(VIP updates every Tue & Wed at noon,
one week early)

410
00:14:04,220 --> 00:14:09,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

411
00:14:09,180 --> 00:14:12,400
(Behind-the-Scenes)

412
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,510
This is awesome.

413
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:15,340
Woah.

414
00:14:15,560 --> 00:14:16,500
This is awesome.

415
00:14:16,520 --> 00:14:18,890
Welcome, everyone, to our home.

416
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:21,590
You can hear the sea.

417
00:14:21,600 --> 00:14:23,550
The sea's right there!

418
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,790
I want to run over.

419
00:14:24,790 --> 00:14:25,940
This is great.

420
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:28,100
Will you swim?

421
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,200
Will people swim here?

422
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:30,970
Will people swim?

423
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,070
I'll swim now. Let's go!

424
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:34,750
Don't scare me.

425
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:37,650
Let me feel it.

426
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:50,740
My gosh.

427
00:14:50,750 --> 00:14:52,380
This feels so great.

428
00:14:56,910 --> 00:14:57,680
This is amazing.

429
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,870
I feel like all my fatigue

430
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:03,150
has been wiped away.

431
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:03,830
It's gone.

432
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:04,510
Totally wiped away.

433
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:06,040
I could just lie down here.

434
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:09,880
A once-in-a-lifetime trip.

435
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,540
Cherish it.

436
00:15:11,710 --> 00:15:12,560
Cherish all of this.

437
00:15:12,560 --> 00:15:14,060
All of it.

438
00:15:14,540 --> 00:15:19,460
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

439
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:21,260
(Behind-the-Scenes: Couples House)

440
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,670
Have you not made
a presentation in a while?

441
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,150
Yeah.

442
00:15:25,150 --> 00:15:26,760
I graduated. Why would I make one?

443
00:15:27,470 --> 00:15:28,780
Let me show you

444
00:15:28,780 --> 00:15:30,140
my presentation masterclass.

445
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:33,110
I'm really good at making them.

446
00:15:34,220 --> 00:15:36,420
(Serious)

447
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:38,070
Are you thinking

448
00:15:38,080 --> 00:15:39,110
about how you want to present it?

449
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,190
I'll just prepare a script

450
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,190
and read it.

451
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,030
Ten minutes for presentation

452
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:45,930
and another ten for Q&A.

453
00:15:45,930 --> 00:15:46,690
Are you nervous?

454
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,090
Not really?

455
00:15:48,330 --> 00:15:49,300
Are you nervous?

456
00:15:49,530 --> 00:15:50,800
A little.

457
00:15:51,020 --> 00:15:52,540
I keep thinking
you're waiting for me here.

458
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:54,040
So I need to finish quickly.

459
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:55,870
Finish it properly

460
00:15:55,880 --> 00:15:57,910
then hurry back.

461
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,310
Hopefully it'll go smoothly.

462
00:16:00,310 --> 00:16:01,080
It will.

463
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:03,500
(Glances)

464
00:16:09,190 --> 00:16:10,900
You need to go out tomorrow.

465
00:16:11,290 --> 00:16:13,390
You promised you'd enjoy
the scenery for me.

466
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,100
It's so beautiful here.

467
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:17,570
I think Beijing is pretty beautiful too.

468
00:16:18,490 --> 00:16:19,500
You can see Beijing every day.

469
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,120
I'll take you around every day later.

470
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:23,390
But only if you're there.

471
00:16:24,400 --> 00:16:25,270
I know.

472
00:16:25,830 --> 00:16:28,040
I was just worried you'd get too tired.

473
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:29,910
I won't.

474
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:36,780
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

475
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:37,340
(Behind-the-Scenes)

476
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:38,150
Hi.

477
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:39,310
You're back.

478
00:16:41,180 --> 00:16:41,820
It's just...

479
00:16:42,660 --> 00:16:43,260
(Motions)

480
00:16:44,050 --> 00:16:44,870
Where are you going?

481
00:16:45,300 --> 00:16:46,460
Outside.

482
00:16:46,460 --> 00:16:47,020
What's wrong?

483
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:47,940
I'm going out.

484
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:52,160
What?

485
00:16:54,330 --> 00:16:55,180
This is

486
00:16:55,360 --> 00:16:56,030
for you.

487
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:57,010
My gosh.

488
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:59,350
And it happens to be blue and black.

489
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,150
Thank you.

490
00:17:00,150 --> 00:17:02,100
You had a blue
and black one too yesterday.

491
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:03,710
Thank you. It's pretty.

492
00:17:04,100 --> 00:17:04,780
(Takes it)

493
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:05,840
I got this because...

494
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:08,520
I think it really

495
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:10,020
suits your style.

496
00:17:10,960 --> 00:17:11,910
What's this?

497
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,930
It's actually a pair of sunglasses.

498
00:17:14,830 --> 00:17:17,270
And I thought the new packaging

499
00:17:17,280 --> 00:17:18,350
looks really cool.

500
00:17:19,420 --> 00:17:20,920
I want to see what's inside.

501
00:17:23,030 --> 00:17:23,960
It looks like this.

502
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,060
Look at it when you get back.

503
00:17:25,760 --> 00:17:26,230
So yeah.

504
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:27,790
Thank you.

505
00:17:27,790 --> 00:17:28,530
My lord.

506
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,120
It's nice.

507
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:42,980
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

508
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:45,170
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Do you want to try the seafood fried rice?

509
00:17:45,170 --> 00:17:46,000
Pass it around.

510
00:17:47,970 --> 00:17:48,690
This is delicious.

511
00:17:48,690 --> 00:17:49,210
Thank you.

512
00:17:53,280 --> 00:17:53,950
Thanks.

513
00:17:57,700 --> 00:17:59,060
(Glances)

514
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,390
I'll hold it down for you.

515
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,540
(Helps)

516
00:18:08,170 --> 00:18:08,680
Here.

517
00:18:09,020 --> 00:18:10,000
Okay. Thank you.

518
00:18:12,010 --> 00:18:12,900
What's this?

519
00:18:12,900 --> 00:18:13,790
Scallop. Do you want one?

520
00:18:13,790 --> 00:18:14,560
I'll have one spring roll.

521
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:16,560
The scallop, right?

522
00:18:20,800 --> 00:18:22,340
(Serving each other)
Have this.

523
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,560
What's this?

524
00:18:24,560 --> 00:18:24,930
It's...

525
00:18:24,930 --> 00:18:25,390
The one just now.

526
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:26,230
I think I had some.

527
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:27,090
Do you like it?

528
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:27,950
It's pretty good.

529
00:18:29,350 --> 00:18:29,950
Cut it up.

530
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:32,380
Did you try the sticky rice?

531
00:18:32,780 --> 00:18:33,700
The sticky rice?

532
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,700
Yeah. I thought it was pretty good.

533
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:36,450
Thanks.

534
00:18:41,580 --> 00:18:42,620
(Glances)

535
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,730
Where should I put this? Here?

536
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,510
Yeah, I'll put it on the spoon.

537
00:18:58,340 --> 00:18:58,910
Beef.

538
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,030
I'll grab some beef.

539
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:02,030
I'll try a small piece.

540
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:04,730
Okay.

541
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:06,120
There's a cat.

542
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:07,990
Can they eat shrimp and stuff?

543
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:08,870
It can eat this fish.

544
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:09,980
What a good kitty.

545
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:11,400
It's acting all shy.

546
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:15,030
It looks like a little leopard.

547
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:22,260
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

548
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:23,670
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Sha Yue'er, sit.

549
00:19:23,670 --> 00:19:24,280
Sit.

550
00:19:27,530 --> 00:19:28,040
Woah.

551
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,120
There's a plate of meat here.

552
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:30,840
Tell me if you can't reach them.

553
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:31,520
I will.

554
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:33,450
I'll get some for you.

555
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:34,860
Sha Yue'er, get me some fish.

556
00:19:34,860 --> 00:19:35,320
Sure.

557
00:19:36,150 --> 00:19:36,830
A little more.

558
00:19:36,830 --> 00:19:38,740
I'll share it with Cao Yiheng.

559
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:40,980
(Serves*1)

560
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,060
(Serves*2)

561
00:19:42,580 --> 00:19:43,180
(Serves*3)

562
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:44,220
Do you eat mushrooms?

563
00:19:44,820 --> 00:19:45,390
Yes.

564
00:19:46,020 --> 00:19:47,300
(Serves*N)

565
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,390
Did you try the sticky rice?

566
00:19:50,130 --> 00:19:50,780
No.

567
00:19:50,780 --> 00:19:52,270
That's so good. You haven't tried it?

568
00:19:52,270 --> 00:19:53,220
Which one?

569
00:19:54,510 --> 00:19:55,600
I'll steal some rice.

570
00:19:58,830 --> 00:20:00,030
Steal some rice.

571
00:20:00,780 --> 00:20:01,710
A buffet.

572
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:05,110
A whole plateful.

573
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:06,550
For you.

574
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:07,790
Thanks.

575
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:08,710
Thank you, Sha Yue'er.

576
00:20:09,180 --> 00:20:09,940
So much.

577
00:20:15,270 --> 00:20:16,190
It's delicious.

578
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:23,100
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

579
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:23,910
(Behind-the-Scenes)

580
00:20:23,910 --> 00:20:25,430
It looks like a heart.

581
00:20:25,430 --> 00:20:26,470
Yeah. Take a picture of it.

582
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:27,390
We must.

583
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:30,340
Cui Kaiyi,

584
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:32,380
we'd like your help.

585
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:33,140
Not a problem.

586
00:20:33,270 --> 00:20:36,020
(Look up)
We'll take a picture of you two.

587
00:20:36,870 --> 00:20:37,510
What's wrong?

588
00:20:37,510 --> 00:20:39,060
Look. A heart!

589
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:40,700
It is.

590
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:41,140
Like that.

591
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:41,980
An abstract one.

592
00:20:42,150 --> 00:20:43,940
Let's take a photo from behind.

593
00:20:44,030 --> 00:20:45,100
I'll take a polaroid for you.

594
00:20:45,270 --> 00:20:47,110
Sure. Can we include the heart?

595
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:48,380
Okay.

596
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,180
Honestly,

597
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:50,860
the wind is making my eyes water.

598
00:20:51,060 --> 00:20:52,020
Are you tearing up?

599
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:52,820
Yes.

600
00:20:55,620 --> 00:20:59,660
Three, two, one.

601
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:02,660
The photo is going to be amazing.

602
00:21:02,990 --> 00:21:04,590
I can't keep my eyes open.

603
00:21:05,020 --> 00:21:05,940
Are we facing the light?

604
00:21:05,940 --> 00:21:06,590
Or is it backlighting.

605
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,150
How should I take it for you both?

606
00:21:08,150 --> 00:21:08,740
We want to stand here.

607
00:21:08,740 --> 00:21:09,580
Stand there.

608
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:10,420
Either works.

609
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:10,980
Or over there?

610
00:21:10,980 --> 00:21:11,740
Let's do it over there.

611
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:13,380
We'll take one here. Thank you.

612
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:16,310
Ready.

613
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:17,860
Wait.

614
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,620
Let me fix my hair.

615
00:21:19,660 --> 00:21:21,180
(Helps fix her hair)

616
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:22,380
Ready.

617
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:25,060
Three, two, one.

618
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:27,580
Thank you.

619
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:28,380
Perfect.

620
00:21:29,470 --> 00:21:30,300
Let's go inside.

621
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:30,860
Okay.

622
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:36,300
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

623
00:21:36,340 --> 00:21:38,660
(Behind-the-Scenes)

624
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:39,710
Anything you want to try?

625
00:21:41,030 --> 00:21:42,710
I'm very scared of the flying one.

626
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:44,180
If two people can do it together...

627
00:21:44,180 --> 00:21:44,700
You and me.

628
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:45,420
Would you be scared?

629
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:46,350
Would it make you feel better?

630
00:21:49,230 --> 00:21:49,780
I'm afraid of heights.

631
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:50,420
Okay.

632
00:21:50,630 --> 00:21:51,510
It doesn't go that high,

633
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:52,780
and it's really steady.

634
00:21:52,780 --> 00:21:54,140
It's not like you'll suddenly drop.

635
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:56,150
You just stay up there, nice and steady.

636
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:57,110
What kind is it?

637
00:21:57,110 --> 00:21:58,020
Paragliding?

638
00:21:58,020 --> 00:21:58,430
Not paragliding.

639
00:21:58,430 --> 00:22:00,140
A boat pulls you along,

640
00:22:00,140 --> 00:22:01,740
and the parachute slowly lifts you up.

641
00:22:01,740 --> 00:22:02,260
It's not scary.

642
00:22:02,260 --> 00:22:03,620
You should try it.

643
00:22:03,620 --> 00:22:04,060
What do you think?

644
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:05,380
Give it a try.

645
00:22:07,350 --> 00:22:08,150
I'll see.

646
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:16,460
Are you still feeling sick?

647
00:22:17,030 --> 00:22:17,950
Feeling any better?

648
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:20,630
If you don't feel well...

649
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:22,260
I'll just close my eyes for a bit.

650
00:22:22,260 --> 00:22:22,710
Don't worry.

651
00:22:22,990 --> 00:22:23,790
No, I mean, if you're

652
00:22:23,790 --> 00:22:24,700
still sleepy later,

653
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:26,180
you can lie down

654
00:22:27,070 --> 00:22:27,950
on the lounge chair

655
00:22:27,950 --> 00:22:28,910
after we get ashore.

656
00:22:30,270 --> 00:22:31,100
Get some rest.

657
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:32,630
Okay.

658
00:22:33,660 --> 00:22:38,620
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

659
00:22:38,990 --> 00:22:39,670
(Behind-the-Scenes)
Hello.

660
00:22:40,030 --> 00:22:40,700
Hello..

661
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:41,780
What're you up to?

662
00:22:41,780 --> 00:22:42,660
Writing my thesis.

663
00:22:43,310 --> 00:22:45,670
I have a thesis defense tomorrow.

664
00:22:45,900 --> 00:22:46,860
Thesis defense?

665
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:48,060
Where?

666
00:22:48,470 --> 00:22:49,550
Back in Beijing.

667
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:50,700
Tomorrow?

668
00:22:51,590 --> 00:22:53,270
I'll be going for two days.
I'll be back on the 18th.

669
00:22:53,270 --> 00:22:55,220
I'm leaving Cao Yiheng in your care.

670
00:22:55,980 --> 00:22:57,140
Babysit him.

671
00:22:57,750 --> 00:22:58,580
This is so sudden.

672
00:22:58,580 --> 00:22:59,990
Yeah. Way too sudden.

673
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:02,820
When are you coming back?

674
00:23:02,820 --> 00:23:03,420
The 18th.

675
00:23:03,780 --> 00:23:05,220
I'll be here in the morning.

676
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:07,940
It's only two days. He's in your care.

677
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:08,780
Stay safe.

678
00:23:10,110 --> 00:23:10,990
You'll do great.

679
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:12,140
I will.

680
00:23:12,140 --> 00:23:13,220
Good luck.

681
00:23:13,220 --> 00:23:14,220
Good luck!

682
00:23:15,860 --> 00:23:17,700
I'll leave him in your care.

683
00:23:17,990 --> 00:23:18,950
We'll keep an eye on him.

684
00:23:19,190 --> 00:23:20,630
He's been sad all day.

685
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:24,430
Separation anxiety again, huh?

686
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:25,950
Nothing I can do.

687
00:23:29,180 --> 00:23:34,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

688
00:23:34,180 --> 00:23:36,740
(Behind-the-Scenes)

689
00:23:36,740 --> 00:23:38,600
How much older are your sisters?

690
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,520
One is three years older,

691
00:23:40,520 --> 00:23:41,640
and one is seven years older.

692
00:23:41,640 --> 00:23:43,440
Any generation gap between you all?

693
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:43,960
Nope.

694
00:23:44,800 --> 00:23:45,680
That's nice.

695
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,280
You have family around.

696
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:48,100
Yeah.

697
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:50,960
Do you usually go to the movies alone?

698
00:23:52,260 --> 00:23:53,060
Rarely.

699
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:55,600
What kind do you like?

700
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:57,720
Comedy, romance, or family drama?

701
00:23:58,100 --> 00:23:58,640
Comedy.

702
00:23:59,040 --> 00:23:59,400
And also

703
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:01,100
Hong Kong, China movies.

704
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:01,760
You don't really watch family

705
00:24:01,760 --> 00:24:03,080
or romance movies, do you?

706
00:24:04,780 --> 00:24:05,700
Yeah.

707
00:24:05,700 --> 00:24:06,880
Lesser compared to the others.

708
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:09,560
You mostly watch romance movies.

709
00:24:09,560 --> 00:24:11,000
No. I rarely watch them.

710
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:14,600
If we are watching one together,

711
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,320
would you be fine
with watching anything?

712
00:24:17,140 --> 00:24:17,540
Yeah.

713
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:19,040
Anything is fine.

714
00:24:23,620 --> 00:24:25,100
(Thinking)

715
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:26,770
How much do you still hold back?

716
00:24:26,770 --> 00:24:27,220
(Asks)

717
00:24:27,800 --> 00:24:29,280
I don't think I hold back much

718
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:30,720
when it's just the two of us.

719
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:34,160
When we're with everyone else,
I always feel like...

720
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:35,540
Should be more polite.

721
00:24:35,540 --> 00:24:36,340
More proper.

722
00:24:39,100 --> 00:24:40,100
What does that mean?

723
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:41,760
Nothing.

724
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:42,400
Are you like that too?

725
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,480
Of course.

726
00:24:43,480 --> 00:24:44,520
Not so much now.

727
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:45,880
I feel like you can do
whatever you want.

728
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:48,880
Don't overthink it.

729
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,480
We're pretty comfortable
with everyone now.

730
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,240
Yeah.

731
00:24:54,060 --> 00:24:59,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

732
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:00,460
(Behind-the-Scenes)

733
00:25:00,460 --> 00:25:01,020
Yu Xiaoyang

734
00:25:01,280 --> 00:25:01,680
Yes.

735
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:02,620
Who am I?

736
00:25:02,620 --> 00:25:03,620
You are...

737
00:25:03,940 --> 00:25:05,940
(Thinking)

738
00:25:06,280 --> 00:25:07,060
Liang Xiaofang.

739
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:08,760
Liang Xiaofang?

740
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:09,680
- That works too.
- Liang Xiaofang.

741
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:17,540
Sorry.

742
00:25:17,540 --> 00:25:18,560
I'm sorry.

743
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:21,840
You stepped on my toe.

744
00:25:23,200 --> 00:25:23,820
Let me see.

745
00:25:25,200 --> 00:25:26,080
It feels fine.

746
00:25:26,620 --> 00:25:27,140
Really?

747
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:29,800
I didn't feel any pain
when you stepped on it.

748
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:33,240
Let's sit for a bit.

749
00:25:33,340 --> 00:25:33,800
Okay.

750
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:34,600
Take a seat.

751
00:25:34,620 --> 00:25:35,020
Here.

752
00:25:36,060 --> 00:25:37,180
It's so hot.

753
00:25:39,840 --> 00:25:40,840
I want to take off my glasses.

754
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:44,560
How do I look? This spot.

755
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:45,520
(Leans in)
Don't move.

756
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:46,440
There are two marks here.

757
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:47,480
Can you close your eyes?

758
00:25:47,480 --> 00:25:48,600
Let me check my reflection.

759
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:54,880
Okay. You can open them now.

760
00:26:01,280 --> 00:26:02,560
How could you be this pretty?

761
00:26:05,140 --> 00:26:10,100
(Behind-the-Scenes 12)

762
00:26:10,100 --> 00:26:12,260
(Behind-the-Scenes: Heart Signal)

763
00:26:12,340 --> 00:26:13,180
Do you think love

764
00:26:13,180 --> 00:26:15,900
is purely emotional
with no rationality involved at all?

765
00:26:15,900 --> 00:26:17,340
I think at the beginning,

766
00:26:17,340 --> 00:26:19,080
your feelings for someone
are purely emotional,

767
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,640
because you can't bring logic into it.

768
00:26:21,160 --> 00:26:22,680
So in the early stages,

769
00:26:22,680 --> 00:26:24,620
I focus on trying to get to know you.

770
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:26,420
So

771
00:26:26,420 --> 00:26:27,640
you take it one step at a time.

772
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:30,160
Yes. In the beginning.

773
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:31,340
Because you need to know

774
00:26:31,340 --> 00:26:32,560
if they even want to get to know you.

775
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:34,700
By the middle stages, I realize

776
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:36,780
that you're someone who overthinks
and gets scared easily.

777
00:26:38,480 --> 00:26:40,340
Once I have
a basic understanding of you,

778
00:26:40,340 --> 00:26:42,040
I'd feel that given your personality,

779
00:26:42,040 --> 00:26:44,820
those actions were actually
positive signs to me.

780
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:47,340
You'd be thinking

781
00:26:47,340 --> 00:26:49,200
how you can build
on those positive signals,

782
00:26:49,720 --> 00:26:51,980
or how we can get
to know each other better.

783
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:54,600
And I'd also be willing
to make some compromises.

784
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:59,100
I get it, bro.

785
00:27:00,620 --> 00:27:01,420
Alright, sis.

786
00:27:06,700 --> 00:27:11,660
(Behind-the-Scenes 13)

787
00:27:11,920 --> 00:27:13,100
(Behind-the-Scenes)
We can call each other every night.

788
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,060
Don't be sad.

789
00:27:18,060 --> 00:27:19,020
I'm not.

790
00:27:19,140 --> 00:27:20,460
Hugs.

791
00:27:20,460 --> 00:27:21,960
Don't be upset, okay?

792
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:23,920
I'm not upset.

793
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:27,460
Good boy.

794
00:27:30,060 --> 00:27:31,620
I want to stay with you too.

795
00:27:32,840 --> 00:27:35,640
I've gotten so used to having you
by my side these past few days.

796
00:27:35,980 --> 00:27:36,940
(Lock gazes)

797
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,080
It's only for two days.

798
00:27:38,260 --> 00:27:39,060
I'll be right back.

799
00:27:39,220 --> 00:27:40,140
I'll fly there

800
00:27:40,140 --> 00:27:41,160
and fly right back.

801
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:44,560
But if you miss me
or are worried about me,

802
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:45,520
just tell me.

803
00:27:46,880 --> 00:27:49,200
I'll call you right away.

804
00:27:49,580 --> 00:27:51,460
(Moves closer)

805
00:27:51,960 --> 00:27:52,480
Okay.

806
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:53,340
Yeah.

807
00:27:53,340 --> 00:27:54,240
I'll call you at night.

808
00:27:55,180 --> 00:27:55,840
In the future too.

809
00:27:55,840 --> 00:27:57,880
Call me anytime when you miss me.

810
00:27:57,880 --> 00:27:59,100
I will.

811
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:00,340
That's just how I am.

812
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:03,420
That's great. Me too.

813
00:28:03,420 --> 00:28:04,160
Call me anytime.

814
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:06,580
Okay.

815
00:28:08,620 --> 00:28:13,580
(Behind-the-Scenes 14)

816
00:28:13,620 --> 00:28:15,180
(Behind-the-Scenes)

817
00:28:15,180 --> 00:28:17,100
Hello.

818
00:28:17,880 --> 00:28:18,960
There's food too.

819
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:19,740
There is.

820
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:20,760
Do you want to eat?

821
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:22,600
I'm fine. Depends if you want some.

822
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:23,800
So you kind of do.

823
00:28:24,100 --> 00:28:25,600
Let's see what looks good.

824
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:28,480
I wonder if they have ice cream.

825
00:28:30,160 --> 00:28:31,320
There's this coconut.

826
00:28:31,320 --> 00:28:32,340
Yeah. This too.

827
00:28:32,560 --> 00:28:33,520
Let's see what they order.

828
00:28:33,760 --> 00:28:34,460
Go forward.

829
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:38,720
See what you want to eat.

830
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,560
(Blocks)

831
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:40,600
I'm confiscating this.

832
00:28:41,300 --> 00:28:42,100
Let's go.

833
00:28:43,360 --> 00:28:44,200
Let's go over there.

834
00:28:44,560 --> 00:28:45,480
Over there? Okay.

835
00:28:46,480 --> 00:28:47,300
Look at the menu.

836
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:48,100
Decide what you want.

837
00:28:50,880 --> 00:28:51,880
What do you want to eat?

838
00:28:53,060 --> 00:28:53,900
This one.

839
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:55,800
Okay. One fried banana with ice cream.

840
00:28:56,360 --> 00:28:56,580
This one.

841
00:28:56,580 --> 00:28:57,140
I want this one.

842
00:28:57,140 --> 00:28:57,980
One fried chicken.

843
00:28:57,980 --> 00:28:58,920
Yes.

844
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:00,180
Pick one more.

845
00:29:00,180 --> 00:29:01,240
The one you picked.

846
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,520
Sure. We'll have one of those.

847
00:29:02,960 --> 00:29:04,200
Coconut sago.

848
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:05,460
Okay.

849
00:29:06,080 --> 00:29:07,240
How do I pay?

850
00:29:08,380 --> 00:29:09,300
Wait.

851
00:29:10,400 --> 00:29:11,480
Let me.

852
00:29:12,040 --> 00:29:12,640
I scanned the QR.

853
00:29:12,640 --> 00:29:13,440
I scanned it.

854
00:29:14,000 --> 00:29:15,600
(Blocks)
I really did. It's done.

855
00:29:16,760 --> 00:29:18,080
Let's do rock-paper-scissors.

856
00:29:18,080 --> 00:29:18,940
(Same old rule)

857
00:29:18,940 --> 00:29:19,580
No.

858
00:29:20,180 --> 00:29:20,680
Okay.

859
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:24,200
Thank you. Let's go.

860
00:29:24,260 --> 00:29:29,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 15)

861
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:30,020
(Behind-the-Scenes)

862
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:31,080
Let's see what we can do.

863
00:29:31,340 --> 00:29:31,940
Arm wrestling.

864
00:29:32,460 --> 00:29:32,980
Let's do it.

865
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:36,040
You're drinking mine, aren't you?

866
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:37,520
I don't know.

867
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:39,200
That's definitely not yours.

868
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:41,320
I grabbed the wrong one.

869
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:42,000
Sorry.

870
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:42,920
I'm really sorry.

871
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:44,180
I'll wipe it.

872
00:29:44,180 --> 00:29:45,360
I'll make it up to you.

873
00:29:48,740 --> 00:29:49,500
How about this?

874
00:29:49,500 --> 00:29:50,520
Chen Hewen, use all your strength,

875
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:51,660
and she'll use both hands.

876
00:29:51,660 --> 00:29:52,540
Okay. Let's try it.

877
00:29:56,540 --> 00:29:58,460
Three, two, one.

878
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:02,160
Come on!

879
00:30:02,160 --> 00:30:03,960
Move your hand over here.

880
00:30:03,960 --> 00:30:04,760
Come on.

881
00:30:05,600 --> 00:30:06,440
Put some muscle into it.

882
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:08,640
But Sha Yue'er has some muscle
in her forearms.

883
00:30:08,640 --> 00:30:09,480
Look at her forearms.

884
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,040
I have muscles in my upper arms too.

885
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,000
Mr. Chen, you won.

886
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:16,200
Mr. Chen is now

887
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:17,880
the reigning champion.

888
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:19,320
Liang Xiaoyu, do you want to challenge him?

889
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:19,840
Liang Xiaoyu, try it.

890
00:30:19,840 --> 00:30:20,960
I don't want to challenge him.

891
00:30:21,720 --> 00:30:23,120
How about you two do it?

892
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:24,200
Let's do it.

893
00:30:24,720 --> 00:30:26,000
Right hand first.

894
00:30:27,320 --> 00:30:28,480
Move over here.

895
00:30:28,920 --> 00:30:29,640
Let me watch them.

896
00:30:29,640 --> 00:30:30,600
This should be fun.

897
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:32,360
Watch them play.

898
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:35,060
This is worth watching.

899
00:30:35,340 --> 00:30:36,360
So fun to watch.

900
00:30:36,360 --> 00:30:36,720
Come on.

901
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:37,800
This is worth watching.

902
00:30:38,140 --> 00:30:39,540
Three, two, one.

903
00:30:42,840 --> 00:30:43,360
Well.

904
00:30:43,360 --> 00:30:44,160
Let's use the left hand.

905
00:30:44,160 --> 00:30:44,560
Try the left.

906
00:30:44,860 --> 00:30:45,780
So quick.

907
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Left hand. Three, two, one.

908
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:48,080
Does anyone want to make a prediction?

909
00:30:48,380 --> 00:30:48,900
My left hand is too weak.

910
00:30:48,900 --> 00:30:50,880
This is the difference
between lefties and righties.

911
00:30:52,100 --> 00:30:57,060
(Behind-the-Scenes 16)

912
00:30:57,100 --> 00:31:37,900
(Behind-the-Scenes)

913
00:31:37,940 --> 00:31:42,900
(Behind-the-Scenes 17)

914
00:31:42,900 --> 00:31:45,640
("Weekend Crush" early access preview)
It's our anniversary.

915
00:31:45,840 --> 00:31:47,080
Yes. One month.

916
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:52,840
You start drawing.
I'll just go grab something.

917
00:32:06,120 --> 00:32:07,300
I'm going to the bathroom.

918
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:08,100
Go ahead.

919
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,520
What is he doing?

920
00:32:16,600 --> 00:32:17,960
How are you? Any better?

921
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:19,800
What have you drawn?

922
00:32:20,160 --> 00:32:20,840
How is it?

923
00:32:21,800 --> 00:32:23,640
I think yours looks better than mine.

924
00:32:26,520 --> 00:32:27,080
Stargazing room.

925
00:32:27,300 --> 00:32:27,840
Yes.

926
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:29,360
It really looks like it.

927
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:31,160
The hot pot we missed that day.

928
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:31,580
Yes.

929
00:32:32,240 --> 00:32:33,040
Delicious.

930
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,280
A very unique stargazing room.

931
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:38,760
There's a star.

932
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:39,640
So pretty.

933
00:32:40,600 --> 00:32:41,840
It looks better than that one.

934
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:44,020
Does it look good?

935
00:32:44,020 --> 00:32:44,840
Yes.

936
00:32:47,560 --> 00:32:48,960
(Picking Cui Kaiyi up for school)
Let's report to the school.

937
00:32:48,960 --> 00:32:50,760
So what's my role?

938
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:53,760
Just hold the umbrella steady.

939
00:32:54,040 --> 00:32:55,280
The princess' study buddy.

940
00:32:59,340 --> 00:33:00,540
My student card.

941
00:33:01,680 --> 00:33:02,620
Got everything?

942
00:33:02,620 --> 00:33:03,260
Yup.

943
00:33:03,260 --> 00:33:04,560
Let me see your card.

944
00:33:05,700 --> 00:33:06,580
(Shows card)

945
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:09,480
We're going to get some food.

946
00:33:09,480 --> 00:33:10,560
Capital Medical University welcomes you.

947
00:33:11,620 --> 00:33:14,140
Bye bye.

948
00:33:16,300 --> 00:33:18,300
=Heart Signal (China Version) S9=

949
00:33:18,300 --> 00:33:19,740
(SVIP updates every Mon & Tue at noon)

950
00:33:19,740 --> 00:33:21,060
